European Union Finance and economy  ministers hope to clinch by the end of  the year an agreement on a common  approach to new rules to preempt bank  crises following talks in brussels what  was really a unanimous unanimous  position it was that we must find an  agreement in the console before the end  of the year as it was decided by the  European Council but it is also the  feeling of the Member States of my  colleagues that it should be done that  and that it can be done the EU  presidency has tasked a working group to  take forward negotiations on the  proposals for the so-called single  resolution mechanism and single bank  resolution fund the aims to help a  struggling credit institution or  investment firm to recover from any  shock in an orderly manner preserving  its operations and minimizing the  possibility of taxpayer losses the  proposals are a key part of the e used  banking Union The ministers also sought  to reach a political agreement on rules  governing savings taxation a large  majority of nations supported the plan  which would oblige authorities to  exchange information so that interest  payments made in one nation to people  from another EU state are taxed under  the laws of their country of residence  the goal is to help fight tax evasion
 

